 weren't  charged under the bus and ruin their  reputation or reveal classified  information if you send that up to the  hill I guarantee you it'll get out well  what about the part about the early part  of the investigation are you confident  bar and or a Senate committee is going  to get to the bottom I'm pretty sure  there was already an inspector general  in the Justice Department looking at  that particular problem that was related  to the deputy in the FBI who was  dismissed it's worth a look and I think  the Inspector General in the Justice  Department is already looking at that  and I think the Attorney General's  within it right to do that the president  said today it was an attempted coup  illegal takedown of a president and  treason agree with them look I I think  it's a molar report is something the  president ought to be happy about he  basically said what the president was  hoping to hear and I think once it's  revealed as much of it as we can legally  be revealed the president should be  applauding it Senate Watchers there are  a lot of them say your agenda in the  Senate is pretty limited restricted  mostly to confirming nominees not robust  fair that's partially true because the  Democratic House is not likely to take  up our best ideas and we're not likely  to take up theirs on the other hand  personnel is important to Supreme Court  justices 30 Circuit Court judges the  most in the first two years of any  administration in history we've done  seven more circuits now that's 37 we  have 53 district judges backed up these  are lifetime appointments they're going  to make a huge impact on the country in  the future now that we've modified the  rules in a way that will allow us to  expedite these appointments we're going  to do all of the district judges  that's not unimportant that's going to  have the longest impact on the country  of anything we do legislatively one of  the few things you've had major votes on  and you mentioned it is to criticize  