 is there anything we're  heading into this election season we're  always one election away from solving  big things it seems is there any chance  of bipartisan deals on drug prices  possibly infrastructure if we can deal  with how to pay for it we've been to all  been talking about infrastructure  including the president for a couple of  years now if you want to do a really  significant large infrastructure bill we  need to have a lot of straight talk from  everybody on both sides about how you're  gonna pay for it  aggression we desperately need some  immigration legislation the president's  entirely correct about the crisis of the  border and the fact that our immigration  laws do not allow us to deal with the  crisis at the border I would hope that  finally after years of gridlock on this  and by the way it's important to point  out that in 2009 and 2010 with the  Democrats control the entire government  they never brought up immigration reform  never when they owned it it's finally  time for us to step up and not only  solve the crisis at the border but do  some changes in the immigration laws  that are sensible that's stealing this  summer yes we have to do that and will  will tackle that at some point  which Democratic presidential candidate  do you fear the most you know I'm not  gonna answer that question I'll tell you  this I think any the Democrat who  ultimately wins the nomination is  probably going to say oh of course I'm a  capitalist but I think what we need to  look at is what they're advocating not  what they call themselves and any  Democrat who's sympathetic to packing  the Supreme Court getting rid of the  electoral college the green New Deal  medicare-for-all is in my view taking  America in the direction of socialism  and do you think you'll be pushing  another Supreme Court nominee through  who knows if there's a vacancy we will  all right senator thanks very much thank  you

